  "text": "I met with a high level Google ad strategist today, the kind that actually works at Google headquarters in San Francisco, and the most important number we discussed about these subject clients isn't actually their Google ads. We went through two client accounts with the strategist from Google. We kept coming back to lifetime value compared to what it costs to get the customer. The target is a customer worth about three times what you paid for. Once you know what a customer is worth over the years or your lifetime value, you know how much you can afford to pay for one. Stop judging ads by cost per click. Judge them by what the customers they bring are worth. If you want the simple version of how to think about this, comment value and I'll send it to you.",
